Status: DONE
Milestone: Consistent local visual identity
Dependencies: vr-59

Purpose:
  Replace the blue-backed logo with a transparent head, purple hair and pink
  lipstick; make the README identity larger with distinctive Verona lettering.

Tasks:
  Preserve the face-mesh concept and author the requested transparent artwork.
  Choose fitting redistributable typography and preserve its license/source.
  Regenerate the README lockup, app logo, favicon and all existing ICO sizes.
  Verify actual alpha, small-size legibility, local routes and native decoding.
  Update branding documentation, chapter, journal, issue/Project and push.

Acceptance criteria:
  Only the head is visible outside the README wordmark; no blue square remains.
  Hair is purple and lips pink; README displays large artwork beside Verona.
  Every current app/browser icon derives from the same transparent master.
  Wordmark does not depend on network fonts or an installed end-user typeface.
  Existing README speech hero and gallery remain unchanged.
  No live head/manager restart, private data publication or release/tag rewrite.

